---
import Layout from '../../layouts/CostmateLegal.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="CostMate — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the CostMate app by Obura: what data the app handles and how."
>
  <h1>CostMate — Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: August 27, 2026</p>

  <p>
    CostMate ("the app") is a product-costing tool for small manufacturers,
    published by Obura. This policy explains what data the app handles and how.
  </p>

  <h2>Data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data.</strong> When you create an account we store your
      email address and a hashed password. If you sign in with Google, we
      receive your email address and basic profile information from Google; we
      never see your Google password.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>App content you create.</strong> The business details, materials,
      products, recipes, prices, equipment, expenses, notes and photos you
      enter are stored so the app can calculate your costs and sync your data
      across sessions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local preferences.</strong> Theme and language choices are stored
      only on your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Purchase data (only if you subscribe).</strong> If you buy the
      optional Pro subscription, we process your subscription status and store
      receipt — never your card or bank details. See "Payments and
      subscriptions" below.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do NOT do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No advertising, and no advertising or analytics SDKs.</li>
    <li>
      No selling, renting, or sharing of your data with third parties for their
      own purposes. The only third parties that process data on our behalf are
      our infrastructure providers (Supabase, Google sign-in, and — only if you
      subscribe — RevenueCat and your app store).
    </li>
    <li>No collection of contacts, location, call logs, or SMS.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where data is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Account data and app content are stored on Supabase (our database and
    authentication provider), protected by row-level security so each account
    can only access its own data. Traffic between the app and the server is
    encrypted (HTTPS). Google sign-in is processed by Google (see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Payments and subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    CostMate offers an optional Pro subscription. Payments are processed
    entirely by the app store you bought it from — Google Play on Android, the
    App Store on iOS — and we never see your card or bank details. Subscription
    status is managed by
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/">RevenueCat</a>, our
    subscription infrastructure provider, which receives a pseudonymous user
    identifier and purchase information (product, price, store receipt) solely
    to validate purchases and keep your Pro status in sync. If you never
    subscribe, no payment data is processed at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Permissions the app uses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Internet</strong> — required to sync your data.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Camera / photos</strong> — only if you choose to attach a photo
      to a material, product, or your business logo. Photos are used for
      nothing else.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is kept for as long as your account exists. You can permanently
    delete your account and all associated data at any time from within the
    app: <strong>Settings → Account → Delete account</strong>. Deletion is
    immediate and removes your account, business data, and uploaded photos from
    our systems. If you can no longer sign in, see
    <a href="/costmate/delete-account/">how to request deletion</a> or contact
    us at the address below.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>CostMate is a business tool and is not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the updated version will be published at this
    address with a new "last updated" date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or data deletion requests:
    <a href="mailto:comporell@gmail.com">comporell@gmail.com</a>
  </p>

  <p class="muted">
    See also: <a href="/costmate/terms/">Terms of Service</a> ·
    <a href="/costmate/delete-account/">Delete your account</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
